{"lauren:Can I come without a book this week?":"c790121a79fb8d74ba760c352192dd7c62bd4be2b31d370d644cf3fc54d92166","siren:A professional body calls its guidance voluntary, while requiring members to explain departures during renewal. Defenders see accountable discretion; critics see an obligation whose sanctions are merely displaced. Both reject a rigid checklist.":"8178ae5b482da5bbf2ddc06fe657dd22729b25e6eddd341b75f805d89ced32e5","lauren:There is agreement that inaction is consequential, but no shared inference about the authority to proceed. A narrowly bounded interim measure might address urgent risks without presenting the consultation as a mandate it did not establish. Any decision should specify its expiry, enforceable safeguards and how absent voices will influence reconsideration.":"5558e3422aebbdc8da8142c003a1652fe9ab9c6a340fd892d1f6b0669367bac3","siren:An online shop plans to make express delivery the default. A small test found fewer abandoned baskets but did not record delivery complaints. Customers must actively select the cheaper option.":"ca6997a77af565f2c155762fefe165454062dc4c098b024966449af34b1b748d"}